    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS744/senior-business-analyst-online-programme-management-111916-0726": {
      "title": "Senior Business Analyst",
      "description": "Senior Business Analyst - Online Programme Management (111916-0726) at University of Warwick This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Senior Business Analyst - Online Programme Management (111916-0726) University of Warwick - Information & Digital Group Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: Competitive Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 26th August 2026 Closes: 25th October 2026 Job Ref: (111916-0726) Location: University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Duration: Fixed-term contract for 16 months About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Pete Hampshire, Recruitment Manager, at Pete.Hampshire@warwick.ac.uk . As a Senior Business Analyst within the Information and Digital Group (IDG), you will play a key role in delivering the University of Warwick’s Online Programme Management (OPM) initiative, a major transformation supporting the University’s online learning strategy and the development of high-quality digital education. Working at the forefront of early-stage programme delivery, you will translate strategic intent into clear, actionable requirements, helping to shape solutions and lay the foundations for sustainable change. You will lead Discovery activities to define business needs, map current and future states, and provide evidence-based recommendations to inform decision-making across a complex and evolving landscape. Operating as part of a programme team, across multiple workstreams, you will collaborate with senior stakeholders, academic departments, and professional services to bring clarity, structure, and momentum to a high-profile transformation programme. This role offers a unique opportunity to influence how online and digital education is designed and delivered at Warwick, particularly suited to individuals who thrive in ambiguity and can operate effectively at both strategic and operational levels. About You You will bring significant experience of business analysis in complex environments, with the confidence to influence at senior levels and across diverse stakeholder groups. You are skilled at applying structured analysis to deliver clarity and actionable insight across an evolving landscape. Your communication and relationship‑building skills enable you to work effectively across academic and professional services communities. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description as a PDF below. JD - Senior Business Analyst - Online Programme Man (111916).pdf – 108KB Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Technical Web Manager (Maternity Cover) Delivery Manager (Infrastructure) Senior Applied Engineer Digital Risk and Resilience Manager Principal RID (Lead Cyber Security Developer) Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
