    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS738/delivery-manager-110113-0526": {
      "title": "Delivery Manager (110113-0526)",
      "description": "Delivery Manager (110113-0526) at University of Warwick This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Delivery Manager (110113-0526) University of Warwick - Information & Digital Group - Portfolio Delivery Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £47,389 to £56,535\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 26th August 2026 Closes: 25th October 2026 Job Ref: (110113-0526) Location: University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Duration: Fixed-term contract for 18 months About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Pete Hampshire, Recruitment Manager, at Pete.Hampshire@warwick.ac.uk . Are you tempted by joining a top 10 UK University as it celebrates 60 years of commitment to innovation and impact, backed by pioneering research, challenging teaching and a drive to find new solutions to the complex challenges facing our region and the world? Are you motivated by the opportunity to shape digital experiences at a leading UK university? At Warwick, we are proud of our reputation for innovation, impact, and delivering real-world change — and our digital services are central to that ambition. The Information & Digital Group (IDG) is driving a major transformation of how the University designs, builds and delivers its web and digital platforms. As part of this, we are investing in the evolution of our web estate — improving usability, accessibility, performance and scalability across services used by thousands of students, staff and external audiences every day. We are looking for a Delivery Manager to play a critical role in this work. Why Join Us? Be part of a forward-thinking team driving digital innovation in higher education. Work on cutting-edge technologies that directly impact thousands of staff and students. Collaborate in a supportive, inclusive environment that values creativity and continuous improvement. Enjoy excellent benefits, flexible working, and the opportunity to grow your career at a world-class institution. This is an opportunity to: Shape the future of Warwick’s web and digital services. Work in a complex, intellectually stimulating environment. Deliver change that has a visible impact across the University community. About You You are an experienced Delivery Manager who thrives in complex, fast-paced environments where priorities evolve and clarity must be actively shaped. You bring a proven ability to lead delivery across multidisciplinary teams, working confidently with technical specialists, product leads, and senior stakeholders to ensure progress is structured, transparent, and focused on outcomes. You are comfortable navigating ambiguity, making informed decisions, and maintaining momentum across multiple workstreams. You build strong relationships quickly, communicate clearly, and are able to challenge constructively to drive the best outcomes. Above all, you take ownership — bringing accountability, and a pragmatic approach to delivery that balances rigour with flexibility. This is not a passive delivery role. You will be expected to: Drive progress and momentum across complex delivery environments. Establish clarity where ambiguity exists and shape delivery approaches accordingly. Manage dependencies, risks and competing priorities across teams and suppliers. Ensure that delivery is aligned to strategic objectives and delivers measurable value. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description as a PDF below. JD Delivery Manager (110113).pdf – 144KB Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Assistant Director, Academics Principal RID (Lead Cyber Security Developer) Executive Dean - Faculty of Society and Business Head of Alliances Executive Dean of Education MIC Limerick Campus Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
