    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTD099/senior-research-technician": {
      "title": "Senior Research Technician",
      "description": "Senior Research Technician at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Senior Research Technician University of Warwick - School of Life Sciences Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £31,236 to £34,610\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 1st October 2026 Closes: 29th October 2026 Job Ref: 355 About the Role We are looking for an enthusiastic research technician with molecular biology skills to join a small team studying plant cell biology. We have several projects focused on how plant organelles and the cytoskeleton are organised during different developmental contexts. We routinely perform a variety of molecular biology techniques, plant transformation and live-cell imaging and corresponding image analysis. You will work closely with the group leader and PhD students and would be recognised as a contributor on the work you support. About the group You will join the McKenna group in the School of Life Sciences at the University of Warwick. The candidate will work in a team of scientists and collaborate with group members to make discoveries. Regular opportunities will be provided for presentation of the candidate's work, together with bespoke career-mentoring. The McKenna lab shares lab space with the groups of Professor Lorenzo Frigerio, Professor Murray Grant and Professor Richard Napier and we frequently share resources and, expertise. Any requests for further information about the role can be directed to Joe McKenna ( joe.mckenna@warwick.ac.uk ). For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description ( link here ). About You We are looking for someone to provide technical support to PhD researchers and the principal investigator undertaking research projects. The successful candidate will be required to perform various routine and higher-level molecular biology techniques in the lab including cloning (PCR, gel electrophoresis, DNA purification, restriction reactions, ligation reactions, Goldengate assembly, bacterial transformation and culture, plasmid purification, and Sanger sequencing), genotyping (collecting material, genomic DNA extraction, PCR, and gel electrophoresis), genetic transformations, as well as general plant husbandry. Opportunities are available for the individual to perform live-cell imaging and protein biochemistry techniques as required. The ideal candidate would have competency in a range of multidisciplinary molecular biology techniques including cloning (for example, PCR, gel electrophoresis, DNA purification, restriction digests and ligation, Golden Gate assembly, bacterial transformation and culture, plasmid prep), and routine genotyping from sample collection through gDNA extraction to PCR, genetic transformations, cell imaging and protein biochemistry, as well as general plant husbandry of Arabidopsis and N. benthamiana. Most importantly, we are looking for someone who is genuinely curious about the science, engages with the current lab research and with plant cell biology more broadly, and is motivated to develop their own expertise over the course of the role. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try again. Ok Ok Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you create this PhD alert we will email you a selection of PhDs matching your criteria. When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy apply to this service. Any personal data you provide in setting up this alert is processed in accordance with our Privacy Notice Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you create this PhD alert we will email you a selection of PhDs matching your criteria. When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy apply to this service. Any personal data you provide in setting up this alert is processed in accordance with our Privacy Notice I would like to receive email communication from jobs.ac.uk relating to Company News I would like to receive email communication from jobs.ac.uk relating to Conferences, Meetings and Events Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Lecturer in Biochemistry (Maternity Cover) Senior Postdoctoral Research Scientist in AI for Outbreak Response Lecturer in Pathobiology Research Fellow in Nutrition - Research, Policy and Impact Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
