    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTF172/mechanical-maintenance-manager": {
      "title": "Mechanical Maintenance Manager",
      "description": "Mechanical Maintenance Manager at University of Warwick This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Mechanical Maintenance Manager University of Warwick - Estates - Maintenance Operations - Mechanical Services Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £48,337 to £57,666\n                                                                                        per annum. Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 9th October 2026 Closes: 18th October 2026 Job Ref: 390 About the Role The Mechanical Maintenance Manager is part of Estates Maintenance Operations and reports to the Head of Maintenance Operations. The role leads a multidisciplinary in-house mechanical maintenance team and oversees specialist contractors delivering services across the University estate. The post works closely with other Maintenance teams, Estates colleagues, capital and minor works teams, customers, suppliers and contractors to maintain statutory compliance, service continuity and the long-term reliability and efficiency of mechanical assets. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description (link here) . About You You will lead and manage the Mechanical Services section and specialist maintenance contractors, ensuring that statutory, planned and reactive maintenance is delivered safely, cost effectively and in accordance with agreed service standards and key performance indicators. The role is accountable for the operation and maintenance of complex mechanical building services across the University estate, including heating, ventilation, environmental systems and associated infrastructure, and for functional compliance relating to natural gas, pressure systems, local exhaust ventilation, F-Gas, water systems and bulk storage. About the Department Mechanical Services and the wider Maintenance team is a collaborative environment where team members are encouraged to grow. There is opportunity to work on a wide variety of equipment across the Campus. How to Apply To apply please complete your essential personal details and attach a CV and cover letter by the closing date stated. We will review applications throughout the advertising period and may contact shortlisted candidates before the closing date. We therefore encourage interested applicants to submit their application as early as possible. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early should we receive a sufficient number of suitable applications. Please ensure your CV includes your most recent employment experience along with any additional relevant experience and education history. Your cover letter should detail your motivation for applying for the role as well as detailing how you meet the essential and desirable criteria. The interviews will be held on a date to be confirmed. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Research Development and Communications Coordinator Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Grounds Operative Housekeeping Assistant Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager MEP Operations Manager Cleaner Porter Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
