    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTF394/assistant-campus-cleaning-services-manager": {
      "title": "Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager",
      "description": "Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager University of Warwick - Estates – Campus Cleaning Services Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £27,241 to £30,986 Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 9th October 2026 Closes: 18th October 2026 Job Ref: 241 About the Role This is a re-advertisement, previous candidates need not apply. We have a fantastic opportunity for an Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager to join the Campus Cleaning Services team working in our Non Residential, PM team. We are looking for an individual to assist in leading the team to achieve quality standards, maintain systems and safety procedures and to deliver a cost effective, efficient and customer focused Assistant Management. To support and deputise for the Campus Cleaning Services Manager. Flexibility is Essential for this role. Some weekends and evenings working will be required throughout the year depending on business needs. The role is campus based. Please note the usual hours, subject to change: Mon 11.30am - 7pm, Tues/Wed 2pm - 10pm, Thurs 12.30pm - 8.30pm, Fri alternates beween 12.30pm - 8.30pm and 2pm - 10pm. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description (link here) . About You We are looking for a person with extensive management experience who: Has led large teams and knows how to motivate and organise them effectively Can plan and allocate resources efficiently throughout the year Has experience managing budgets and procurement Understands quality control and can address performance issues Knows health and safety regulations related to cleaning Can handle multiple tasks and deadlines Provides excellent customer service to staff, students and visitors Communicates well with other team members and direct reports Can work flexibly, including some late evenings and weekends when needed If you are a practical person, results driven leader looking for a hands-on management role, we would love to hear from you. About the Department For more information about Campus Cleaning Services please see our website: Campus Cleaning Services How to Apply To apply please complete your essential personal details and attach a CV and cover letter by the closing date stated. We will review applications throughout the advertising period and may contact shortlisted candidates before the closing date. We therefore encourage interested applicants to submit their application as early as possible. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early should we receive a sufficient number of suitable applications. Please ensure your CV includes your most recent employment experience along with any additional relevant experience and education history. Your cover letter should detail your motivation for applying for the role as well as detailing how you meet the essential and desirable criteria. The interviews will be held on a date to be confirmed. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your