    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTH558/recruitment-operations-manager": {
      "title": "Recruitment Operations Manager",
      "description": "Recruitment Operations Manager at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Recruitment Operations Manager University of Warwick - People - People Operations Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £48,337 to £57,666\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 16th October 2026 Closes: 25th October 2026 Job Ref: 452 About the Role This is an exciting opportunity to join the team on a fixed-term basis, providing cover during a colleague's secondment. The role is available until 31 December 2027. As a Recruitment Operations Manager at the University of Warwick, you will play a pivotal role in overseeing the end-to-end recruitment operations across the University. You will be responsible for designing, developing, and implementing recruitment practices that not only attract diverse talent but also enhance the Warwick brand. This role requires strong leadership to manage and coach a recruitment team, ensuring best practices are followed in every stage of the recruitment process. Additionally, you will have a key responsibility in improving recruitment policies and procedures, promoting diversity, and ensuring compliance with current recruitment legislation. You will be a critical link between the recruitment team, senior stakeholders, and the People Operations function, working closely to provide seamless service delivery and a positive candidate experience. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description ( link here ). About You You are a highly experienced HR professional with a background in recruitment or talent management. Ideally, you hold a CIPD qualification or equivalent and have a deep understanding of recruitment policies, processes, and relevant legislation. Your exceptional interpersonal and communication skills allow you to influence and build strong relationships with stakeholders at all levels. You are proactive, customer-focused, and always looking for ways to improve services. Your leadership experience includes managing teams, developing talent, and driving continuous improvement. You thrive in a complex environment, thinking critically and strategically to find effective solutions. With your dedication to professional growth, you are passionate about creating a positive impact within the University’s recruitment processes. You are also eager to contribute to an inclusive and diverse workforce, ensuring recruitment practices reflect these values. For further information regarding the skills required for this role please see the personal specification section of the attached job description. About the Department The People Operations team we are committed to nurturing our talent and fostering a thriving community. Our team ensures a supportive, inclusive and innovative working environment for all university colleagues. Come and join the team to help contribute to the success of our globally renowned institution. Our purpose is to enable our people to thrive in an ever-changing environment to make a better world. We want to be a People function that puts people at the heart of what we do and achieves a great employee experience. It is a place where you feel valued, are able to have your say and be heard, are proud to work and thrive, growing and achieving your potential. Closing Date: Sunday 25 October 2026, 11:59 pm The interviews will be held on a date to be confirmed. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Clerk of Works Manager Commercial Lead History of Art MPhil/PhD Global Sustainable Development MPhil/PhD Hispanic Studies MPhil/PhD History MPhil/PhD Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Unitemps Branch Manager (2134) Deputy Director of Human Resources Recruitment Consultant (2135) HR Administrator (Salaried) HR Adviser (Fixed Term) Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
