    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTG454/finance-manager": {
      "title": "Finance Manager",
      "description": "Finance Manager at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Finance Manager University of Warwick - Finance - Estates Finance Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £48,337 to £57,666\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time, Part Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 14th October 2026 Closes: 27th October 2026 Job Ref: 427 About the Role For informal queries about the role, please contact Rob Morgan, Chief Finance Officer (Estates), at Robert.W.Morgan@warwick.ac.uk . We will consider applications for employment on a part-time basis, despite the position being advertised as full-time. We welcome applications from candidates seeking a minimum of 30 hours per week. Join the University at a pivotal moment as we deliver two of our most significant capital investment projects, with annual budgets of more than £150m over the next three years. This is a high-profile opportunity to play a central role in the financial management of major developments that will help shape the future of our estate and support world-class teaching, research and collaboration. You will work closely with the University Capital Accountant, programme sponsors, Estates Directors and senior Finance colleagues, gaining excellent exposure across the organisation. The role offers the chance to take ownership of broad responsibilities across the projects, including financial reporting, cashflow forecasting, contractor liaison, payment certification and commercial risk mitigation. Your work will directly inform University treasury planning and support confident decision-making across major project delivery. By ensuring valuations, certifications and payments are processed smoothly, you will help maintain strong supplier relationships, support commercial control and keep major works moving at pace. Embedded within the University’s delivery team, you will build valuable expertise in capital and project accounting while developing trusted relationships across Estates, Procurement, Finance AP, Treasury and Group Accounting. This is an exciting opportunity for someone who wants to combine technical financial expertise with meaningful business partnering on a programme of real scale and visibility. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description ( link here ). About You You’ll bring strong capabilities across the following key skillsets: Production and presentation of financial reports Stakeholder engagement and communication Analytical and problem-solving Excitement and enthusiasm in being embedded within the delivery of the largest capital investment in UoW’s history Fully qualified accountant (e.g. CIPFA, CIMA, ACCA) A strategic mindset with the ability to balance operational priorities with long-term organisational objectives. If you are looking for a role where your financial insight, stakeholder skills and commercial judgement can make a tangible impact, we would welcome your application and look forward to hearing how you can contribute to the successful delivery of the Connect capital programme. Closing Date: Tuesday 27 October 2026, 11:59PM (UK) Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Clerk of Works Manager Recruitment Operations Manager Commercial Lead History of Art MPhil/PhD Global Sustainable Development MPhil/PhD Hispanic Studies MPhil/PhD Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Research Finance Project Coordinator Accommodation Commercial Performance Manager Chief Executive Officer Commercial Lead Procurement Manager Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
