    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTH367/clerk-of-works-manager": {
      "title": "Clerk of Works Manager",
      "description": "Clerk of Works Manager at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Clerk of Works Manager University of Warwick - Estates - Maintenance Operations - Zonal Operations Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £48,337 to £57,666\n                                                                                        per annum. Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 16th October 2026 Closes: 28th October 2026 Job Ref: 444 Closing Date: Wednesday, 28 October 2026, 11:59 pm. About the Role To lead, manage and develop the Clerk of Works Team, providing a coordinated inspection and quality-assurance service across capital projects, minor works and maintenance activities. The postholder will act as the principal point of contact for incoming inspection requirements, assess their priority and complexity, and allocate work according to risk, programme requirements, professional discipline and staff competence. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description (link here) . About You We are seeking an experienced and technically proficient professional to lead and manage the Clerk of Works/site inspection team, ensuring the consistent delivery of high-quality inspection, reporting and assurance across multiple construction and maintenance projects. The postholder will provide technical leadership, allocate resources in line with project risks and priorities, and oversee compliance with drawings, specifications, contractual requirements, Building Regulations, relevant legislation and University standards. They will monitor inspection findings, identify recurring quality issues, oversee the resolution of significant defects and ensure that unresolved concerns relating to safety, quality, compliance or contractual obligations are appropriately escalated. A key aspect of the role will be to lead the Clerk of Works function in supporting fire and life-safety compliance, working closely with Fire Safety and Health & Safety colleagues to address issues relating to fire stopping, fire doors, passive fire protection, asbestos and building fabric. Through strong leadership, technical expertise and collaborative working, the postholder will play a vital role in maintaining high standards of construction quality, safety and regulatory compliance across the University’s estate. About the Department For more information about the Estates department please see our website: Estates | University of Warwick How to Apply To apply please complete your essential personal details and attach a CV and cover letter by the closing date stated. We will review applications throughout the advertising period and may contact shortlisted candidates before the closing date. We therefore encourage interested applicants to submit their application as early as possible. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early should we receive a sufficient number of suitable applications. Please ensure your CV includes your most recent employment experience along with any additional relevant experience and education history. Your cover letter should detail your motivation for applying for the role as well as detailing how you meet the essential and desirable criteria. The interviews will be held on a date to be confirmed. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Recruitment Operations Manager Commercial Lead History of Art MPhil/PhD Global Sustainable Development MPhil/PhD Hispanic Studies MPhil/PhD History MPhil/PhD Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Head Groundskeeper Electrician Facilities Coordinator Commercial Lead Security Operations Manager Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
    },
    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTH171/engineering-school-of-engineering-mphil-phd": {
      "title": "Engineering (School of Engineering) MPhil/PhD",
      "description": "Engineering (School of Engineering) MPhil/PhD at University of Warwick Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice PhDs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice PhDs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Engineering (School of Engineering) MPhil/PhD University of Warwick – School of Engineering With 93% of our complete REF2021 submission ranked as ‘world-leading’ or ‘internationally excellent,’ Warwick’s School of Engineering is one of the leading unified engineering schools in the UK. Our MPhil/PhD in Engineering will give you the skills and knowledge needed to thrive as an independent research professional. The MPhil/PhD in Engineering at the University of Warwick offers students the opportunity to undertake a substantial piece of independent research within one of the UK’s leading unified engineering schools. Based in Warwick’s School of Engineering, the MPhil/PhD course allows students to immerse themselves in a vibrant and supportive postgraduate research community. With over 150 postgraduate research students and more than 40 postdoctoral researchers, our School fosters an active environment for innovation and discovery. As a general engineering department, we are uniquely positioned to support multi-disciplinary research across a broad range of topics. Our researchers collaborate with academic colleagues across the University and with a wide network of external partners—including SMEs, large corporations, NHS Trusts, charitable organisations, and other universities—to address real-world engineering challenges. Students register in the first instance for the degree of MPhil unless otherwise approved by the Board of Graduate Studies. Subject to satisfactory progress, registration may be upgraded to the degree of PhD.  If you prefer to complete the MPhil, this is a two-year registration. Master of Philosophy (MPhil) To satisfy the requirements of the degree of MPhil a thesis shall constitute an original contribution to knowledge. The thesis shall be clearly and concisely written and well-argued and shall show a satisfactory knowledge of both primary and secondary sources. In addition, it shall contain a full bibliography and, where appropriate, a description of methods and techniques used in the research. The maximum length of the thesis is 60,000 words. A student must attend an oral examination, which shall cover the thesis itself and the field of study in which the thesis has been written. The examiners may also require the student to take a written and/or practical examination. The student must complete satisfactorily the oral examination and written and/or practical examination, in order to satisfy the requirements for the degree. Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) To satisfy the requirements of the degree of PhD, a thesis must constitute a substantial original contribution to knowledge and is, in principle, worthy of peer-reviewed publication. The thesis shall be clearly and concisely written and well-argued and shall show a satisfactory knowledge of both primary and secondary sources. It shall contain a full bibliography and, where appropriate, a description of methods and techniques used in the research. The maximum length of the thesis is 70,000 words. A student must attend an oral examination (viva voce), which shall cover the thesis itself and the field of study in which the thesis has been written. The examiners may also require the student to take a written and/or practical examination. The student must complete satisfactorily the oral examination and written and/or practical examination, in order to satisfy the requirements for the degree. For more information and to apply please click the 'Apply' button above. Qualification Type: PhD Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Funding amount: Not Specified Hours: Full Time, Part Time Placed On: 15th October 2026 Expires: 15th January 2027 Reference: P-H1Q2 Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Show all PhDs for University of Warwick … Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): PhD tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
    },
    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTG840/customer-services-library-assistant-x2": {
      "title": "Customer Services Library Assistant x2",
      "description": "Customer Services Library Assistant x2 at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Customer Services Library Assistant x2 University of Warwick - Library Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £25,528\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 15th October 2026 Closes: 1st November 2026 Job Ref: 423 About the Role For informal enquiries, please contact Inga Vai (Customer Services Coordinator) at Inga.vaicaityte@warwick.ac.uk . Post 109251 pattern: Friday 8am-2:45pm; Saturday - Sunday 8am - 2:30pm. Post 109245 pattern: Thursday 1:15pm-8pm; Friday 1:30-8p; Saturday 1:30pm-8pm. This also applies to those weeks which include bank holidays and statutory/customary days, where you will be rostered to work as required. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description (link here) . About You What does the successful candidate look like? We are looking for outstanding candidates to join our Customer Services team. You will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellent customer service, using strong interpersonal skills to work with a diverse range of people. You will be willing to learn, keen to take on new challenges and be able to work in a constantly evolving, busy customer focused environment. You will be highly motivated and enthusiastic. For further information regarding the skills required for this role please see the personal specification section of the attached job description. About the Department This is a unique opportunity to join the Library following the recent transformation of our services and launch of a new strategy. We are looking for inspiring, credible, and authentic team players. This is an opportunity to join this front facing Library team responsible for enquiry handling and customer support in both the Main Library and University Archive (Modern Records Centre). The successful candidates will provide support for a range of face to face and virtual enquiry services. It’s an opportunity to support the operational delivery and development of excellent frontline customer services, including all the Library’s diverse customer communities. How to Apply To apply please complete your essential personal details and attach a CV and cover letter by the closing date and time stated. We will review applications throughout the advertising period and may contact shortlisted candidates before the closing date. We therefore encourage interested applicants to submit their application as early as possible. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early should we receive a sufficient number of suitable applications. Please ensure your CV includes your most recent employment experience along with any additional relevant experience and education history. Your cover letter should detail your motivation for applying for the role as well as detailing how you meet the essential and desirable criteria. The interview date will be confirmed at a later stage. Closing Date: Sunday 1 November 2026, 11:59PM (UK) Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD 