    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTF907/applied-linguistics-mphil-phd": {
      "title": "Applied Linguistics MPhil/PhD",
      "description": "Applied Linguistics MPhil/PhD at University of Warwick Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice PhDs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice PhDs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Applied Linguistics MPhil/PhD University of Warwick – Applied Linguistics The MPhil/PhD in Applied Linguistics is expertly designed for those who want to make a real difference to society through research. The University of Warwick's Department of Applied Linguistics, ranked 9th in the UK for Linguistics The Complete University Guide 2024, will nurture your academic and professional development. PhD researchers are individually mentored by academic supervisors from the beginning of their journey. They also participate in weekly research seminars in Year One to develop their skills and understanding in relation to research issues and approaches, methods of data collection and analysis, and research ethics. For more information and to apply please click the 'Apply' button above. Qualification Type: PhD Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Funding amount: Not Specified Hours: Full Time, Part Time Placed On: 15th October 2026 Expires: 15th January 2027 Reference: P-X3ZN Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Show all PhDs for University of Warwick … Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): PhD tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Adve