    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTF975/philosophy-and-literature-phd": {
      "title": "Philosophy and Literature PhD",
      "description": "Philosophy and Literature PhD at University of Warwick Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice PhDs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice PhDs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Philosophy and Literature PhD University of Warwick – Doctorate of Philosophy (PhD) Our Philosophy and Literature PhD is a leading interdisciplinary research programme which will enable you to develop individual research expertise in philosophy and literature. Drawing on the breadth and depth of research expertise in philosophy and literature, distinctively covering all areas of both analytic and continental philosophy, you will engage in focused research under close expert supervision, as part of a vibrant research community. The skills and subject knowledge you will gain, including through our curated professional development activities, provide ideal preparation for further research or teaching. You can also get involved in the various scholarly activities organised by the interdisciplinary Centre for Research in Philosophy, Literature and the Arts Link , as well as those of our other research centres (the Centre for Research in Post-Kantian European Philosophy, the Warwick Mind and Action Research Centre, and the Centre for Ethics, Law and Public Affairs) Teaching and learning You will produce an 80,000-word thesis that can provide the basis for professional publication. You will contribute to department’s vibrant research community by taking part in work-in-progress seminars and the activities of the department’s research centres. In addition to regular expert supervisions, we provide a suite of professional development activities, designed to foster your skills in researching, writing, and teaching philosophy, including our core PhD seminar as well as wider career development guidance. Additionally, you will attend relevant postgraduate seminars, including modules on our taught MA programmes. For more information and to apply please click the 'Apply' button above. Qualification Type: PhD Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Funding amount: Not Specified Hours: Full Time, Part Time Placed On: 15th October 2026 Expires: 15th January 2027 Reference: P-V7P1 Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Show all PhDs for University of Warwick … Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): PhD tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
